# omarchy-settings ships the same files on every architecture when its source
# has this file: the recipe stops leaving drop-ins out of the aarch64 package.
# Each platform-specific file below, by its path in this source, takes its
# decision at runtime instead.
#
# etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/00-omarchy-hooks.conf
#   Sets each platform's HOOKS baseline (omarchy-hw-platform), and leaves alone
#   a Mac whose own mkinitcpio.conf carries asahi or busybox encrypt.
# etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/omarchy_hooks.conf
#   Only filters kms for NVIDIA and handles the vconsole hooks, from the
#   machine's own devices and configuration.
# etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/thunderbolt_module.conf
#   Adds thunderbolt to MODULES only where modinfo finds it as a loadable module.
# etc/limine-entry-tool.d/, default/limine/
#   Read only where Limine and its entry tool are installed.
# etc/systemd/oomd.conf.d/, default/systemd/user/app.slice.d/10-oomd.conf
#   Inert unless systemd-oomd runs (install/config/enable-services.sh,
#   migration 1785424256).
# default/systemd/zram-generator.conf.d/90-omarchy.conf,
# etc/sysctl.d/99-omarchy-sysctl.conf, etc/tmpfiles.d/omarchy-zswap.conf
#   Swap on zram everywhere: the installer provides zram-generator on x86_64,
#   install/omarchy-aarch64.packages on aarch64.
# etc/modprobe.d/omarchy-usb-autosuspend.conf
#   Applies where usbcore is a module; a kernel that builds it in ignores it.
